<title>GERMANY: German oilseed area seen in line with trade accord.</title>
<headline>German oilseed area seen in line with trade accord.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German oilseeds producer lobby UFOP on Friday issued oilseeds area estimates for 1997 showing Germany was in line with limits under the international Blair House trade accord.</p>
<p>The total oilseeds area of 951,203 hectares was broken down as follows -- winter rapeseed 861,362 hectares (777,190 ha in 1996), spring rapeseed 55,662 ha (76,435), sunseed 34,179 (43,758).</p>
<p>Non-food areas consisted of 108,000 ha of rapeseed and 3,000 ha of sunseed.</p>
<p>The total 111,000 ha non-food area as well as 7,000 ha of land owned by small farmers excluded from the Blair House rule had to be deducted from the total.</p>
<p>The resulting 833,203 ha compared with an 836,099 ha limit allocated to Germany for food use under the European Union-U.S. deal dating back to 1992.</p>
<p>Farmers in EU countries have to pay collective penalties if they overshoot their national Blair House limits.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
